   205	# SDD Workflow & Worktree Policy
   206	
   207	---
   208	
   209	## Git Configuration
   210	
   211	The Git Parrot Flow (FEAT-187) uses three long-lived branches:
   212	
   213	- **`main`** — tagged releases only. Hotfixes land here via PR;
   214	  no feature work ever bases on `main`.
   215	- **`staging`** — release candidate branch. Cut from `dev` when the
   216	  team decides to freeze a release. Receives `main → staging` syncs
   217	  automatically (via `.github/workflows/sync-down.yml`); the
   218	  `dev → staging` direction is a manual cut at freeze time.
   219	- **`dev`** — integration branch for all feature work. Default base
   220	  for `type: feature` flows.
   221	
   222	**Flow types** (FEAT-145, refined by FEAT-187):
   223	- `feature` — base is `dev` (default) or `staging` (during a release
   224	  freeze). NEVER `main`.
   225	- `hotfix` — base is `main` (mandatory).
   226	
   227	**Sync-down automation** (FEAT-187): `.github/workflows/sync-down.yml`
   228	listens for pushes to `main` and tries to fast-forward `staging` and
   229	`dev`. When fast-forward is not possible, it opens a sync PR against
   230	the lagging branch. `/sdd-done --sync-down` is the manual fallback for
   231	the same operation.
   232	
   233	**`/sdd-done` NEVER pushes to or opens a PR against `main`** —
   234	hotfix PRs are user-initiated. After the user merges the hotfix into
   235	`main`, the Action propagates the change to `staging` and `dev`. If
   236	the Action fails (or the user is offline), run
   237	`/sdd-done <FEAT-ID> --sync-down` to do the same locally.
   238	
   239	**Recommended branch protection**: `main` (and `staging` once in use)
   240	should require PRs, passing CI, and signed commits. Not configured
   241	declaratively in this repo — set via GitHub repo settings.
   242	
   243	- **Worktrees branch from `base_branch`** (which `/sdd-task` and `sdd-worker` ensure HEAD is on before creating the worktree). Hotfix worktrees branch from `main`; feature worktrees branch from `dev` or `staging` (during a release freeze).
   244	
   245	## Worktree Creation
   246	
   247	> **CRITICAL**: Do NOT use `claude --worktree`. It branches from the repo's default
   248	> branch (`main`), which does not contain SDD artifacts.
   249	>
   250	> Always create worktrees manually from the current branch:
   251	
   252	```bash
   253	# Standard pattern: create worktree from current branch
   254	git worktree add -b <branch-name> .claude/worktrees/<worktree-name> HEAD
   255	```
   256	
   257	> **Carve-out (FEAT-466): "from the current branch … `HEAD`" is shorthand,
   258	> not the rule.** The actual rule is **worktrees branch from `base_branch`**
   259	> (§ Git Configuration above). `HEAD` only works as shorthand when `HEAD`
   260	> already *is* the intended base — true for `/sdd-task` and `sdd-worker`,
   261	> which always `git checkout "$BASE_BRANCH"` immediately beforehand. It is
   262	> **not** true for a hotfix: `sdd-research.md` branches
   263	> `hotfix-<JIRA-KEY>-<slug>` explicitly from `origin/main`, regardless of
   264	> what branch happens to be checked out in the main repo at the time (a
   265	> hotfix must never inherit unreleased `dev` commits — this is the FEAT-466
   266	> root cause, PR #1250). When base and `HEAD` might differ, name the ref
   267	> explicitly:
   268	> ```bash
   269	> # Feature — from the base branch (dev, or staging during a freeze)
   270	> git worktree add -b feat-<id>-<slug> .claude/worktrees/feat-<id>-<slug> origin/dev
   271	> # Hotfix — ALWAYS from origin/main, never from HEAD/dev
   272	> git worktree add -b hotfix-<JIRA-KEY>-<slug> .claude/worktrees/hotfix-<JIRA-KEY>-<slug> origin/main
   273	> ```
   274	
   275	### Quick reference
   276	
   277	```bash
   278	# From dev (most common)
   279	git checkout dev
   280	git worktree add -b feat-014-videoreel-visual-changes \
   281	  .claude/worktrees/feat-014-videoreel-visual-changes HEAD
   282	
   283	# From another feature branch (sub-features)
