   124	### Adversarial Second Opinion
   125	
   126	Use an external CLI agent as an independent perspective for adversarial
   127	code reviews, design opinions, brainstorming, research cross-checks, and
   128	implementation sanity checks. The reviewer is **`codex` (OpenAI)**.
   129	
   130	> **`agy` (Google Gemini / Antigravity) MUST NOT be used as a reviewer.**
   131	> It was removed as an option on 2026-09-01 after it returned a fabricated
   132	> review: invented a 188-test pytest run with test names that do not exist
   133	> in the branch under review, then terminated with `Error: timeout waiting
   134	> for response`. A reviewer that hallucinates passing evidence is worse
   135	> than no reviewer, because its output reads like corroboration. Do not
   136	> re-add it, and do not fall back to it when `codex` is unavailable — when
   137	> there is no external reviewer, say so and rely on a Claude subagent.
   138	>
   139	> This bans `agy` **as a reviewer only**. It is unrelated to the
   140	> `google_coding` dev-loop backend, which drives the same `agy` binary as a
   141	> *coding* agent (`dispatchers/google_coding.py`) and is untouched.
   142	
   143	Rules:
   144	- Never feed the reviewer your reasoning, justification, or preferred
   145	  conclusion. Give it only the diff, the requirement, and the question.
   146	  Supplying your conclusions produces ratification, not review.
   147	- Treat reviewer output as advisory. For every substantive finding,
   148	  explicitly mark it as `CONFIRM` (adopt), `REJECT` (with reason), or
   149	  `ESCALATE`.
   150	- Never silently concede to the reviewer and never silently drop a finding.
   151	- Run each reviewer call as a full background agent session. Typical runtime
   152	  is 30 seconds to 2 minutes; do not call it per edit or from hooks.
   153	- For parallel perspective, use one Claude subagent and one background
   154	  reviewer session with the same neutral brief, then synthesize agreements
   155	  and disagreements.
   156	- **Verify the reviewer's evidence before believing it.** If it claims a
   157	  test run, a file, or a symbol, spot-check that the thing exists. Treat an
   158	  unverifiable claim as no finding at all, and say the review was
   159	  unusable rather than reporting it as a pass.
   160	
   161	**Detection:**
   162	```bash
   163	if command -v codex &>/dev/null; then REVIEWER="codex"
   164	else echo "No external reviewer CLI found"; fi
   165	```

