   119	## Adversarial Cross-Check
   120	
   121	Use an external CLI agent as an **independent second-opinion reviewer** to
   122	catch blind spots that a single-model review may miss. The reviewer is
   123	**`codex` (OpenAI)**.
   124	
   125	> **`agy` (Google Gemini / Antigravity) MUST NOT be used as a reviewer.**
   126	> Removed 2026-09-01 after it returned a fabricated review — an invented
   127	> 188-test pytest run whose test names did not exist in the branch, then
   128	> `Error: timeout waiting for response`. Hallucinated passing evidence is
   129	> worse than no review, because it reads like corroboration. Do not re-add
   130	> it and do not fall back to it: with no external reviewer available, say
   131	> so and rely on a Claude subagent. (Unrelated to the `google_coding`
   132	> dev-loop *coding* backend, which drives the same binary and is fine.)
   133	
   134	### Key Rules
   135	
   136	- **Never feed the reviewer your reasoning or draft review.** Give it only
   137	  the diff/commit, the requirement/acceptance criteria, and a neutral review
   138	  question. Supplying your conclusions produces ratification, not review.
   139	- **Run the reviewer as a background agent session** — each call takes 30
   140	  seconds to 2 minutes. Do not call it per-edit or from hooks.
   141	- **Treat reviewer output as advisory.** For every substantive finding,
   142	  explicitly mark it as:
   143	  - `CONFIRM` — adopt the finding into your review
   144	  - `REJECT` — record why you disagree
   145	  - `ESCALATE` — flag for the user to decide
   146	- **Never silently concede** to the reviewer and **never silently drop** a
   147	  finding.
   148	- **Verify the reviewer's evidence.** If it cites a test run, a file or a
   149	  symbol, spot-check that it exists. An unverifiable claim is not a
   150	  finding — report the review as unusable rather than as a pass.
   151	
   152	### Detection
   153	
   154	```bash
   155	if command -v codex &>/dev/null; then REVIEWER="codex"
   156	fi
   157	```
   158	
   159	### codex commands
   160	
   161	```bash
   162	# Review uncommitted work
   163	codex exec review --uncommitted
   164	
   165	# Review a task branch against the integration branch
   166	codex exec review --base dev
   167	
   168	# Review a specific commit
   169	codex exec review --commit <sha>
   170	
   171	# Design opinion or cross-check with output file
   172	codex exec --sandbox read-only -o artifacts/reviews/<task>-codex.txt \
   173	  "<neutral brief: task context, acceptance criteria, changed files, question>"
   174	
   175	# Follow-up in the same Codex session
   176	codex exec resume --last "<neutral follow-up question>"
   177	```
   178	
   179	### Parallel Perspective Pattern
   180	
   181	For the strongest review, run one Claude review subagent and one background
   182	reviewer session (`codex`) with the **same neutral brief**, then
   183	synthesize agreements and disagreements in the final report.
